  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">219990 FY22 3UN Extension Rapid WASH Emergency Response Cyclone Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">WVUK 100% project. Nampula province. WASH initially targeting 4,200 people in emergencies following cyclone but increased to 9,200 in cost extension A1 to meet the needs of high numbers of Internally Displaced Persons following recent attacks in Nampula and Cabo Delgabo. A NCE extended the project from a March end to April end date A2.
 
 4,200 people affected by emergency situation in Mozambique have protected and reliable access to safe water, sanitation and hygiene facilities and/or a safe and healthy environment, contributing to reduce the risk of transmission for WASH related diseases. Target population/ group(s)
 
 Children and their families affected by emergency situation, with focus on emergency accommodation centres.
 
 Output 1: Water supply.
 
 Indicator 1: Number of people with access to sufficient quantity of safe water (from durable water point)
 
 Total: 2,400
 
 Monthly
 
 Indicator 2: # rehabilitated water points
 
 Total: 8
 
 Monthly
 
 Indicator 3: # rehabilitated water point with a functional Operation &amp; Maintenance system
 
 Total: 8
 
 Monthly
 
 Output 2: Sanitation.
 
 Indicator 1: Number of people with access to appropriate communal
 
 Total : 4,200
 
 4,200 communal
 
 Monthly
 
 Indicator 2: # communal
 
 Total : 84
 
 84 communal
 
 Monthly
 
 Output 3: Hygiene promotion and community engagement
 
 Indicator 1: # of people receiving sanitation and hygiene messages
 
 Total: 4,200
 
 Monthly
 
 Indicator 2: # of families receiving WASH NFI (survival hygiene kits, complete hygiene kits, cholera kit)
 
 Total: 1,680
 
 840 survival / Z complete / 840 cholera
 
 Monthly
 
 Indicator 3: # of caregivers routinely engaged on behaviours for infectious disease prevention and nutrition
 
 Total: 500
 
 Monthly</narrative>
  </description>
